    "number": 36954,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net: make address overlap impossible when relaying addresses",
    "user": {
      "login": "vasild",
      "id": 266751,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2Njc1MQ==",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266751?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vasild",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/vasild/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`CService::GetKey()` didn't include the network in the output. So in theory it would be possible for two IP2 and Tor addresses to have the same output from `CService::GetKey()`.\r\n\r\nThis would have unexpected results when used in the per-peer bloom filter of known addresses - we may wrongfully assume that a peer knows `foo.onion` when we have sent to them `foo.i2p`.\r\n\r\nTo make this impossible - include the network in `CService::GetKey()`.\r\n\r\nAddrman already includes the network separately so it does not need this change. The code would be simplest if addrman also uses `GetKey()` with the network but that would mess the positions of addresses in existent databases (`peers.dat`). So, keep a variant of network-less `GetKey()` for addrman.\r\n\r\nThanks, @l0rinc for pointing me into this. I think it is minor but also the change is minor, so worth fixing IMO.\r\n\r\n",
