      ],
      "message": "net: make address overlap impossible when relaying addresses\n\n`CService::GetKey()` didn't include the network in the output. So in\ntheory it would be possible for two IP2 and Tor addresses to have the\nsame output from `CService::GetKey()`.\n\nThis would have unexpected results when used in the per-peer bloom\nfilter of known addresses - we may wrongfully assume that a peer knows\n`foo.onion` when we have sent to them `foo.i2p`.\n\nTo make this impossible - include the network in `CService::GetKey()`.\n\nAddrman already includes the network separately so it does not need this\nchange. The code would be simplest if addrman also uses `GetKey()` with\nthe network but that would mess the positions of addresses in existent\ndatabases (`peers.dat`). So, keep a variant of network-less `GetKey()`\nfor addrman.",
