      "body": "There are two things here: 1. values for `m_net` that should never be set and 2. ensure that the switch handles all enum values.\r\n\r\nFor example here there are two asserts to handle each one of 1. and 2.:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/edcac28380bbb8409988583b9f1ab32c41f52cac/src/netaddress.cpp#L487-L501\r\n\r\nand here just 1. is checked:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/edcac28380bbb8409988583b9f1ab32c41f52cac/src/netaddress.cpp#L111-L136\r\n\r\nThe new code I added is like in the second example, handling only 1. To handle 2. one must conclude every `case` with a `return` so that the assert after the switch becomes unreachable. This is omitted in places where some work has to be done after the switch.",
